    "name": "x19_fix_closes",
    "trailer": "",
    "_note": "Not a numbered trailer shot. The third belief behaviour: a correction closing a doubled corridor. LIDAR.md 4 found this reads as a PAIR of frames and not as one still; the answer to that is that it is a shot. Two things had to be pushed to make it read at all, and both are recorded rather than hidden: the walk is 43 m each way because the doubling is only as wide as the drift the walk earns, and the crop box is 0.30 m so the ribbon is ground rings and not lower wall. At 27 m and a 0.55 m crop the two records read as ONE WIDE corridor, which is exactly the failure LIDAR.md 4 predicted.",
